      "passed": false,
      "error": "",
      "final_answer": "I\u2019m sorry you received a bag with a broken zipper.\u202fEven though the bag was marked **final sale**, that status does **not** cancel the limited warranty for a qualifying manufacturing defect. A broken zipper is considered a defect, so you can still file a warranty claim for a repair or replacement\u202f(07-warranty.md \u2014 Final-sale products).  \n\nFinal\u2011sale items can\u2019t be returned simply because you changed your mind, but **damaged** final\u2011sale items are eligible for assistance under our Damaged or Wrong Items Policy\u202f(01-returns-policy-current.md \u2014 Exclusions and exceptions).  \n\n**What to do next**\n\n1. Visit the \u201cWarranty Claims\u201d section on our website and start a claim for the bag, describing the broken zipper.  \n2. If you need help with the claim form or have any questions, you can reply here or contact our support team directly\u2014they\u2019ll guide you through the process.\n\nIf you run into any trouble, let us know and we\u2019ll connect you with a human representative.\n\n---",
